nts"},{"surface":"மிகுப்ப","parts":[{"text":"மிகுப்ப","lemma":"மிகுத்தல்","gloss":"to increase"}],"gloss":"to increase"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வாள்","parts":[{"text":"வாள்","lemma":"வாள்","gloss":"sword"}],"gloss":"sword"},{"surface":"அமர்","parts":[{"text":"அமர்","lemma":"அமர்","gloss":"battle"}],"gloss":"battle"},{"surface":"உயர்ந்த","parts":[{"text":"உயர்ந்த","lemma":"உயர்தல்","gloss":"eminent"}],"gloss":"eminent"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நின்","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"தானையும்","parts":[{"text":"தானை","lemma":"தானை","gloss":"army"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"army also"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"சீர்","parts":[{"text":"சீர்","lemma":"சீர்","gloss":"glory"}],"gloss":"glory"},{"surface":"மிகு","parts":[{"text":"மிகு","lemma":"மிகுதல்","gloss":"abundant"}],"gloss":"abundant"},{"surface":"செல்வமும்","parts":[{"text":"செல்வம்","lemma":"செல்வம்","gloss":"wealth"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"wealth also"},{"surface":"ஏந்துகம்","parts":[{"text":"ஏந்துகம்","lemma":"ஏந்துதல்","gloss":"let us praise"}],"gloss":"let us praise"},{"surface":"பலவே","parts":[{"text":"பல","lemma":"பல","gloss":"many"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"many indeed"}]}],"literal":"Having scooped up water so that the long, roaring ocean diminishes / the clouds that move swiftly, assembling in desired places / appearing like a great mountain, their pregnancy maturing / discharging their duty of rain with a suite of roaring thunder / in the hot season when the fertile mountain rains have ceased / like the Ganges river whose bank-battering abundant waters are full, which all mankind goes to realize / as you are a great lord to us and to others / 'bandits without love having killed, plundering the path / those who went are not those who return; without love / to those who crossed the harsh desert where the strong buck bellows / with today's day, a year has passed' saying / with weeping that has lost the spark of her eyes, her strength ruined / my woman who experiences great distress, suffering deep grief, your / wealth obtained by effort, every time she sees, to be amazed / with a broad trunk resembling a palmyra tree, with matured pearls born / a strong male elephant resembling a mountain, holding up high tusks / with a shining forehead plate splendid, on the sides / sounding bells ringing repeatedly, having mounted with pride / desiring to go, I have reached you, O victorious lord / poverty driving me, to give me fame, having come, your / desire bound with generosity, please listen to my request / whether I am capable or not capable, quickly / without looking at and measuring my worth, / please measure your own great worth and give, O lord, always / so that kings feel ashamed, I will return, having smeared sandalwood paste / on my beautiful high chest with many marks / every time glorious jeweled women embrace, to rejoice / in your territory possessing wide space where the morning drum sounds / those who live under the shade of your feet, their good ornaments increasing / your victorious army eminent in sword battles / and your glorious abundant wealth, let us praise many indeed!","translation":"The swift-moving clouds scoop up water from the vast, roaring ocean until it diminishes, gather in desired places, and look like great mountains. As their water-load matures, they discharge their duty of rain with roaring thunder. In the hot season when the rains on the fertile mountains have ceased, the Ganges river is filled with abundant waters battering its banks, where all mankind goes to bathe. Just like that river, you are a great lord of refuge to us and to others. My wife, suffering deep grief and experiencing great distress, has lost the brightness of her eyes from weeping. Her strength ruined, she laments: 'Bandits without mercy kill and plunder on the paths. Those who went are not those who return. To him who crossed the harsh desert where the strong buck bellows, a full year has passed today.' To make her marvel whenever she sees the wealth I bring, I desired to go and have reached you, O victorious lord! I wish to mount a strong male elephant that resembles a mountain, holding up high tusks containing mature pearls, with a broad trunk like a palmyra tree, adorned with a shining forehead plate and bells ringing on its sides, and ride home with pride. Driven by poverty, I have come so that you may give me fame. Please listen to my request bound to your generosity. Whether I am highly capable or not, do not look at my worth to measure your gift; instead, measure your own great generosity and give, O Lord! I will return so that other kings feel ashamed, with sandalwood paste smeared on my beautiful broad chest marked with many spots, to the joy of my glorious, jeweled wife whenever she embraces me. May those who live under the protective shade of your feet in your vast territory, where the morning drum sounds, abound in fine ornaments! May your army, victorious in sword battles, and your glorious wealth be praised for many years!","modern":"ஒலிக்கும் கடலின் நீரை முகந்து கொண்டு, மேகங்கள் திரண்டு, பெரிய மலை போலத் தோன்றி, இடியுடன் மழையைப் பொழிந்து ஓய்ந்தன. மழை பொய்த்த கோடைக் காலத்தில், மக்கள் அனைவரும் சென்று நீராடும் கங்கை ஆற்றின் கரையை முட்டும் வெள்ளம் போல, நீ எமக்கும் பிறருக்கும் புகலிடமாக விளங்குகிறாய். 'வழியில் இரக்கமில்லாத ஆறலைப்பறையர்கள் கொன்று கொள்ளையடிக்கிறார்கள்; சென்றவர்கள் திரும்புவதில்லை; ஆண் மான் கத்தும் அரிய பாலைவனத்தைக் கடந்து சென்ற என் கணவர் பிரிந்து இன்றுடன் ஒரு வருடம் ஆகிவிட்டது' என்று என் மனைவி அழுது கண் ஒளி இழந்து, வலிமை குன்றி, பெருந்துயரால் வருந்துகிறாள். அவள் வியக்கும்படி, பனைமரம் போன்ற தும்பிக்கையும், முத்துக்கள் கொண்ட தந்தங்களும் உடைய, நெற்றிப்பட்டமும் மணிகளும் அணிந்த யானையின் மீது ஏறிப் பெருமிதத்துடன் நான் செல்ல விரும்புகிறேன். வறுமை துரத்த, உனது வள்ளல் தன்மையை நாடி வந்துள்ளேன். எனது தகுதியை ஆராயாமல், உனது பெருந்தன்மையின் அளவுக்கு ஏற்ப எனக்குப் பரிசளிப்பாயாக. மன்னர்கள் நாணும்படி, சந்தனம் பூசிய மார்போடு நான் திரும்பிச் சென்று என் மனைவியைக் கூடி மகிழ்வேன். உனது குடிகள் நலம் பெறவும், வாள் போரில் சிறந்த உனது சேனையும் செல்வமும் பல்லாண்டு வாழ்க!","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Paṭāṇ tiṇai and is a song of request (paricil) addressed to the patron Kumaṇaṉ by the poet Peruñcittiraṉār. The poet describes the desperate state of his wife, who is wasting away in grief, counting the days and years since he left to find wealth. He compares Kumaṇaṉ's boundless generosity to the Ganges river, which remains full of water even during a severe drought when mountain rains fail. The poet requests a grand gift—specifically a majestic elephant—so that he can return home in pride, making other kings feel ashamed of their own smallness and bringing immense joy to his suffering wife. He urges Kumaṇaṉ not to measure the gift by the poet's own worth, but by the king's own infinite capacity for giving. Key words include 'செம்மலை' (great lord), 'அருந்துயர்' (deep grief), and 'வண்மையில்' (generosity).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}